<Project>

  <!-- Hot-path server settings: Server GC + concurrent, DATAS off.

       These live in a .targets file, NOT in Directory.Build.props, on purpose. Props are imported
       before the SDK, where $(OutputType) is still empty, so the same PropertyGroup conditioned on
       'Exe' in Directory.Build.props evaluates to false and silently does nothing — the published
       runtimeconfig.json then carries Server GC (an ASP.NET Core SDK default) with DATAS still ON,
       which is precisely the configuration docs/architecture.md rules out. Targets are imported
       after the SDK, so the condition here sees a real OutputType.

       DATAS ships ENABLED by default with Server GC since .NET 9. It starts at one heap and ramps
       reactively, scheduling full compacting GCs as it adapts — measured 1.16-1.69x regressions on
       latency-sensitive workloads (dotnet/runtime#109047). A fixed-tick game server wants stable
       p99 over a small RSS, so it is switched off deliberately.

       Test projects are excluded: xunit v3 makes them OutputType=Exe too, and the test host's GC
       mode is nobody's contract. Verify with:
         dotnet msbuild src/Pix3.Rooms.Server/Pix3.Rooms.Server.csproj -getProperty:GarbageCollectionAdaptationMode
       and by grepping System.GC.DynamicAdaptationMode in the published runtimeconfig.json. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(OutputType)' == 'Exe' AND '$(IsTestProject)' != 'true'">
    <ServerGarbageCollection>true</ServerGarbageCollection>
    <ConcurrentGarbageCollection>true</ConcurrentGarbageCollection>
    <GarbageCollectionAdaptationMode>0</GarbageCollectionAdaptationMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
